    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        40,
        1010
      ],
      "size": [
        810,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How it works",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "8.0.1",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. Load a clear portrait of the character (more images give a stronger reference: RefMod Bake also takes a folder of images and video frames).\n2. RefMod Bake encodes it through the H3 video VAE and saves a reusable refmod file in models/refmods/characters. Its mods output feeds RefMod Apply directly, so one run bakes and uses the character.\n3. RefMod Apply injects the reference into the H3 conditioning. retention sets how strongly it holds, and the curve controls when it applies during the clip.\n4. Next time, bypass the Bake group and pick the saved file in RefMod Apply's mod_1.\nNeeds: the H3 reference-to-video model, text encoder and the video and audio VAEs."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "1. Load a clear portrait of the character (more images give a stronger reference: RefMod Bake also takes a folder of images and video frames).\n2. RefMod Bake encodes it through the H3 video VAE and saves a reusable refmod file in models/refmods/characters. Its mods output feeds RefMod Apply directly, so one run bakes and uses the character.\n3. RefMod Apply injects the reference into the H3 conditioning. retention sets how strongly it holds, and the curve controls when it applies during the clip.\n4. Next time, bypass the Bake group and pick the saved file in RefMod Apply's mod_1.\nNeeds: the H3 reference-to-video model, text encoder and the video and audio VAEs."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
